  <joint name="dobot_to_laser" type="fixed">
    <!--
      KSJ UC3D scanner coordinate convention (in laser_frame):
        X  = horizontal laser line (3582 pts, 1516mm)
        Y  = arm travel direction  (1533 profiles, 230mm)
        Z  = depth from scanner head (positive = away from scanner, downward toward ground)

      CONFIRMED from log data (X/Y spans in base_link after TF):
        world X span ~0.285m = arm travel (230mm)   → laser_frame X drives world X
        world Y span ~1.36m  = laser line (1516mm)  → laser_frame Y drives world Y
        So the URDF rotation maps: laser_frame X → world X, laser_frame Y → world Y

      In laser_driver.cpp we therefore assign:
        laser_frame x = scanner Y (arm travel, j * y_spacing)   → world X
        laser_frame y = scanner X (laser line, i * x_res)       → world Y (negated by Rx(pi))

      URDF rpy = "pi 0 -2*pi/3" achieves:
        Rx(pi): flips laser_frame Y and Z signs
        Rz(-2pi/3): handles the physical mounting rotation of the scanner

      Measure the actual XYZ offset from Link6 flange to the scanner emission point
      and replace xyz="0 0 0.05" with the real values.
    -->
    <origin xyz="0 0 0.05" rpy="3.1415927 0 2.0944" />
    <parent link="Link6" />
    <child link="laser_frame" />
  </joint>
</robot>